The problem asks us to calculate the sum of $f(P)$ over all $N!$ permutations $P$ of $(1, 2, \ldots, N)$, modulo 998244353.
Here $f(A)$ is formed by concatenating the decimal representations of the elements of $A$ and interpreting the result as an integer.
Let $A = (A_1, A_2, \ldots, A_N)$. Then $f(A) = \sum_{i=1}^N A_i \cdot 10^{L_{i+1} + \dots + L_N}$, where $L_i$ is the number of digits in $A_i$. Wait, let's recheck the definition.
